T0/t0/t1/T1/T2/t2/t3/T3/T4/T5/T6/T7: conjugation for -àr, -ér, '-er, -ír, -ír/is (T0 is indicative present, t0 is T0 for words without vanishing el, t1 is T0 for words with vanishing el, T1 is indicative imperfect, indicative future, subjunctive imperfect, and conditional present, T2 is subjunctive present, t2 is T2 for words ending in /ie/, t3 is T2 for words ending in /je/, T3 is imperative present, T4 is conjugation for -ír/is, T5 is indicative present second singular for stressed third person of '-er, T6 is for padoan vowel lowering for '-er, T7 is stressed root indicative present second singular person interrogative)
L0/L1/L2/L3/L4/L5: conjugation for -àr, -ér, '-er, -ír, -ír/is for third person pronomenal verbs, non-vanishing el (L0 is indicative present, L1 is indicative imperfect, indicative future, subjunctive imperfect, and conditional present, L2 is imperative present, L3 is indefinitive form, L4 is conjugation for -ír/is, L5 is for padoan vowel lowering for '-er)
l0/l1/l2/l3/l4/l5: conjugation for -àr, -ér, '-er, -ír, -ír/is for third person pronomenal verbs, vanishing el (l0 is indicative present, l1 is indicative imperfect, indicative future, subjunctive imperfect, and conditional present, l2 is imperative present, l3 is indefinitive form, l4 is conjugation for -ír/is, l5 is for padoan vowel lowering for '-er)
N0/N1/N2/N3/N4/N5/N6/N7: conjugation for -àr, -ér, '-er, -ír, -ír/is, northern variant (N0 is indicative present, N1 is indicative imperfect, indicative future, subjunctive imperfect, and conditional present, N2 is subjunctive present, N3 is imperative present, N4 is indefinitive form, N5 is indicative present for -ír/is, N6 is for padoan vowel lowering for '-er, N7 is stressed root indicative present second singular person interrogative)
W0: conjugation for -ír, -ír/is, northern variant
W1/w1: infinitive simple for -àr, -ír, -ír/is, lagunar variant (non-vanishing el variant/vanishing el variant)
W2/w2: infinitive simple for -ér, padoan and coxòto variants (non-vanishing el variant/vanishing el variant)
W3/w3: infinitive simple for '-er, padoan and coxòto variants (non-vanishing el variant/vanishing el variant)
W4: infinitive simple for '-er, non-vanishing el variant

xA: irregular verb (re)?andar
xB: irregular verb (re)?av?er, (re)?g(av)?er, ʼv?er
